 The conversation stays inside the portal for now: replies do not send email.
 
+### Staff
+
+A business is served by its staff: the admins and the agents. Both work every
+conversation of the business (`/tickets`), only the admins manage the people.
+The staff of a business are listed under `/api/v1/staff`:
+
+| Endpoint                  | Description                                                       |
+| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `GET /api/v1/staff`       | The staff of the business, oldest first.                          |
+| `GET /api/v1/staff/:id`   | One staff member.                                                 |
+| `PATCH /api/v1/staff/:id` | `{"user": {"role": "admin"}}` or `{"user": {"name": "Al Smith"}}`. |
+| `DELETE /api/v1/staff/:id`| Removes a staff member that never worked on a conversation.        |
+
+Nobody may change their own role or remove themselves, and people that opened or
+answered a conversation stay in the business, so their work does not disappear.
+
+### Invitations
+
+New staff members are invited by email. An admin sends an invitation, the
+invited person opens the link from the mail in the frontend, looks the
+invitation up and answers it:
+
+```http
+POST /api/v1/invitations
+{"invitation":{"email":"sam@example.test","role":"agent"}}
+```
+
+The role is `agent` (the default) or `admin`. The invitation is returned and a
+link to `/accept-invitation?account=acme&token=…` is mailed to the address; a
+shorter spelling of the very same screen (`/accept-invite`) travels with it in
+case a mail client mangles the long one.
+
+The invited person reads the invitation with the token from that link:
+
+| Endpoint                            | Body                                                     |
+| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `GET /api/v1/invitations/:token`    | -                                                        |
+| `POST /api/v1/invitations/accept`   | `{"invitation":{"token":"…","name":"Sam","password":"…"}}` |
+
+Both return the `invitation`; accepting it also returns the new `user`, the
+`account` and a `session`, because the new staff member does not have to verify
+the address that was just invited. The address may not belong to somebody of the
+business yet, and an address is only invited once at a time.
+
+An invitation is `pending` until it is answered, then `accepted`, `revoked` or
+`expired` — it is only good for a week. The admins of the business keep an eye
+on them:
+
+| Endpoint                              | Description                                       |
+| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
+| `GET /api/v1/invitations?status=…`    | Every invitation of the business, oldest first.    |
+| `POST /api/v1/invitations/:id/resend` | A new link replaces the old one, the week restarts.|
+| `DELETE /api/v1/invitations/:id`      | Revokes the invitation, the address may be invited again. |
+
+A revoked invitation cannot be answered anymore, and an accepted one cannot be
+sent again.
+
